# Machine-local tooling, package caches, decompiled reference inspection, build evidence.
#
# The 40 register PROOFS and the 11 PLANT suites are the exception, un-ignored below. Owner
# direction, 2026-09-30, verbatim: *"i need someone else to work on this in parrellel through
# git hub and i need to make sure they have it all but the temp stuff i told you to git ignore"*.
# Those scripts are neither machine-local nor temp -- they are this project's primary
# verification instrument, and a clone without them can run the 13 checkers and none of the 40
# proofs. Everything else under .local/ stays out: a 132 MB nuget cache, 19 MB of decompiler
# binaries, the per-subsystem source inspections, and the one-shot record/ship/fix scripts.
#
# Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so the parent has to be re-admitted a level
# at a time before a negation inside it can match. Same pattern as !.claude/bin/ below.
#
# .local/harness/ joined them at 0.12.62-dev for the same reason. `check-planner-layouts.py` is
# checker FOURTEEN and it runs the planner for real, which is the only thing in this battery that
# can see a feature go absent -- and a checker whose source a clone does not get is a checker that
# silently stops existing. Its bin/ and obj/ stay out; they are build output.

!.local/register/

!.local/register/proof-*.py
!.local/register/plant-*.py
# `build-dependencies.py` joined them at 0.12.79-dev, and it is the third instance of this exact
# defect. `AGENTS.md` and the queue both name it as the ONLY sanctioned way to change the
# dependency blocks -- *never hand-edit them, edit this script and re-run it* -- while the script
# itself was not in the repository. A clone got 293 generated rows and no generator, so the only
# way to change them in a clone was the one way the rule forbids.
!.local/register/build-dependencies.py
# And the same reasoning one directory over, caught before it became the FOURTH instance in one
# day. `.local/qa/` is machine-local scratch, but two of its scripts are instruments rather than
# scratch: the plant that proves the clause-scoped dependency rule can still fail, and the
# measurement that reports whether any living document has drifted back to a false claim. A rule
# whose plant a clone does not get is a rule that silently stops being guarded.
!.local/qa/

!.local/qa/plant-retirement-scope.py
!.local/qa/measure-dependency-claims.py
!.local/harness/
.local/harness/**/bin/
.local/harness/**/obj/
artifacts/
Mod/**/Assemblies/*.dll
Mod/**/Assemblies/*.pdb
*.local.props

